# `actuarial::Triangle::development`

[Back to `actuarial::Triangle`](../Triangle.md)

The column labels.

## Signature

```cpp
const std::vector<std::string> &actuarial::Triangle::development() const noexcept;
```

## What It Does

Returns the labels of the development ages in column order (for example the months since the start of the origin period), or an empty vector when none were given. They must match the number of columns when supplied and have no effect on the estimates.

## Returns

A const reference to a vector of `ndevelopment` strings, or an empty vector.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1: labelled columns

The ages given at construction.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series cumulative = pluss::make_series({100.0, 180.0, 220.0, 240.0,
                                                       110.0, 200.0, 250.0, 0.0,
                                                       120.0, 215.0, 0.0, 0.0,
                                                       130.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0}, {4, 4});
  const actuarial::Triangle triangle = actuarial::triangle::cumulative(cumulative, pluss::series::undefined(), {"2021", "2022", "2023", "2024"}, {"12", "24", "36", "48"});
  for (const auto &d : triangle.development()) out.write(d, " ");
  out.writeln();
}
```

### Example 2: no labels

An unlabelled triangle returns an empty vector.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series cumulative = pluss::make_series({100.0, 180.0, 220.0, 240.0,
                                                       110.0, 200.0, 250.0, 0.0,
                                                       120.0, 215.0, 0.0, 0.0,
                                                       130.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0}, {4, 4});
  const actuarial::Triangle triangle = actuarial::triangle::cumulative(cumulative);
  out.writeln("labels:", triangle.development().size());
}
```

### Example 3: labelling the factors

The age-to-age factor `j` takes the triangle from age `j` to age `j + 1`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series cumulative = pluss::make_series({100.0, 180.0, 220.0, 240.0,
                                                       110.0, 200.0, 250.0, 0.0,
                                                       120.0, 215.0, 0.0, 0.0,
                                                       130.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0}, {4, 4});
  const actuarial::Triangle triangle = actuarial::triangle::cumulative(cumulative, pluss::series::undefined(), {"2021", "2022", "2023", "2024"}, {"12", "24", "36", "48"});
  const auto f = actuarial::operators::chain_ladder()(triangle).age_to_age.items<double>();
  for (std::size_t j = 0; j < f.size(); ++j) out.writeln(triangle.development()[j], "->", triangle.development()[j+1], f[j]);
}
```

### Example 4: a wrong count

The number of labels must equal the number of columns.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto report = [&](const auto &call) {
    try {
      call();
    } catch (const std::exception &e) {
      std::string text(e.what());
      if (const auto cut = text.find("Triggered"); cut != std::string::npos) text.erase(cut);
      while (!text.empty() && text.back() == '\n') text.pop_back();
      out.writeln(text);
    }
  };
  report([&] { (void)actuarial::triangle::cumulative(pluss::make_series({1.0, 2.0, 0.0, 0.0}, {2, 2}), pluss::series::undefined(), {}, {"12"}); });
}
```

